{
  "item": "CAP-P3UNDO-PREDICTED",
  "from": "our code on main, as is, run twice before any oracle read of these steps (the same both times): Edit Section, Custom height, the field and slider as marks-check.mjs drives them, Undo by our top bar button, Escape and the panel opened again. field and slider are what each shows; minVh is the section min-height in vh; open is whether the panel shows. One difference in the steps: after 'panel again' the oracle presses Custom again (a no-op if Custom is still picked), ours presses it only if the slider is hidden.",
  "question": "P3, its two inferred parts: is a field change on Enter one undo step, and a slider pull one undo step on let go? After NaN in the field, does the last number come back when the panel opens again? On Blocks Probe, predictions first.",
